ictims of armed <ei18 attack> , but they do not have the right to <ei19 work> . And today , the right to work is <ei21 equal> to r - the right to survival . Ms. Atimadi <ei22 says> the <ei23 war> has <ei24 created> a nation of widows . Women have <ei25 become> the sole <ei26 support> of their families . Yet , the Taliban have <ei27 forbidden> them to <ei28 work> . She <ei29 says> this <ei30 puts> the very existence of women 's families at risk . She <ei31 says> the plight of women in urban areas is <ei32 greater> than that which exists in rural parts of the country . In cities , such as the capital Kabul , women are totally <ei33 dependent> on international aid for survival . Ms. Atimadi <ei34 says> the women of Kabul <ei35 symbolize> the suffering of all the women in Afghanistan . The aim is to <ei36 bring> in not only the focus on women 's right to education , access to work , but <ei37 look> beyond that and <ei38 look> at the roots of , uh of these problems . These are only the symptoms of the problems that are <ei39 facing> Afghanistan . For women in Afghanistan to be <ei40 able> to <ei41 realize> their rights , there have to be conditions of peace and justice . Ms. Atimadi <ei42 says> that is the primary focus of her group , peace and justice . She <ei43 says> her group is <ei44 appealing> to individuals , to the international community , and to the combatants and people of Afghanistan to <ei45 stop> the <ei46 bloodletting> which has <ei47 torn> the country apart . Lisa Schlein for VOA News , Geneva .", "gold": [], "lang": "eng", "mentions": ["ei2", "ei3", "ei5", "ei6", "ei7", "ei8", "ei9", "ei11", "ei12", "ei13", "ei14", "ei15", "ei16", "ei17", "ei18", "ei19", "ei21", "ei22", "ei23", "ei24", "ei25", "ei26", "ei27", "ei28", "ei29", "ei30", "ei31", "ei32", "ei33", "ei34", "ei35", "ei36", "ei37", "ei38", "ei39", "ei40", "ei41", "ei42", "ei43", "ei44", "ei45", "ei46", "ei47"], "surfaces": {"ei2": "events", "ei3": "organized", "ei5": "leaving", "ei6": "says", "ei7"